                            "Typografie"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "13f216f5-a95c-469c-bd40-fbc364130567",
                                "sense_id": "4d67ea2a-c84c-3fad-a52c-090185ec2316",
                                "text": "Das Doppelkreuz (#) hat viele verschiedene Anwendungen und Funktionen, beispielsweise als Telefontaste unter der 9."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cfc3d350-7c8a-30e8-8154-16c491237bcc",
                        "entry_id": "9faf0333-0e3b-3d38-9eba-a892a97f09ab",
                        "glosses": [
                            "verdoppeltes Versetzungszeichen, das eine Erhöhung um einen Ganztonschritt bewirkt"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Musik"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c4d0c3ba-fa60-4483-a4ba-ac1e06121c77",
                                "sense_id": "cfc3d350-7c8a-30e8-8154-16c491237bcc",
                                "text": "Cis-Dur hat sechs Kreuze und ein Doppelkreuz als Vorzeichen."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b7c1e390-31b2-3e87-b409-acad90a643ba",
                        "entry_id": "9faf0333-0e3b-3d38-9eba-a892a97f09ab",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Stab/Balken mit zwei Querbalken (statt einem bei einem einfachen Kreuz)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "676e0fc0-1c8d-4788-8179-385072f74761",
                                "sense_id": "b7c1e390-31b2-3e87-b409-acad90a643ba",
                                "text": "„863 reisten die Brüder nach Großmähren. Dort führten sie die glagolitische Schrift ein, brachten ihre Übersetzungen und das Doppelkreuz aus Byzanz mit.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"3\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "78e6d186-1310-4823-b479-ea53cfe8565b",
                        "source_entry_id": "9faf0333-0e3b-3d38-9eba-a892a97f09ab",
                        "source_sense_id": "4d67ea2a-c84c-3fad-a52c-090185ec2316",
                        "source_sense_description": "Satzzeichen",
                        "target_lang_word": "number sign",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "number sign",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5d1caaa2-3a7f-372f-9233-f43028e40ee6",
                                        "entry_id": "a6e2ff8b-fc76-3c89-846d-64f2801a7041",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The character # used to represent the word number."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d1fb3896-8b1b-4e2c-9f0c-27a241db5db8",
                                                "sense_id": "5d1caaa2-3a7f-372f-9233-f43028e40ee6",
                                                "text": "The number sign (#) is used when the number to be printed represents cents only, and is designed to prevent any one from placing a false figure in the dollar position on the check."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "63bcd480-3e1c-4461-8201-67c5951e6af7",
                                                "sense_id": "5d1caaa2-3a7f-372f-9233-f43028e40ee6",
                                                "text": "367. Characters.—The upper case of the first row of keys contains characters. You will have frequent occasion to use the quotation mark or ditto (\"), the underscore (_), the apostrophe ('), parenthesis left [(] and right [)], and the hyphen (-). The number sign (#), the dollar sign ($), percent sign (%), the ampersand or \"and\" sign (&), and the asterisk (*) are mostly used in reports and tabulating work."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7d655c1e-4b58-485e-9bdb-8ef7216c70e3",
                                                "sense_id": "5d1caaa2-3a7f-372f-9233-f43028e40ee6",
                                                "text": "New material which has been inserted on the page is indicated by the number sign (#). Where more than one or two lines have been inserted in consecutive sequence the number sign (#) appears above and below the material inserted rather than appearing on each individual line of the group. In cases where an entirely new listing is included the number sign (#) appears in the first line of the page. The appearance of three number signs (###) indicates the omission of material from that page."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a05f242c-e00b-4e7e-a69b-2d04183c5921",
